    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/D---6-East-16th-Street/SAS-Media-Studies-Film-Office-Tech-Assistant_JR109345": {
      "title": "SAS Media Studies Film Office Tech Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-28\nPosted: Posted 8 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nParsons School for Design, a division of The New School, seeks Student Assistants in the Media Studies Film Office within the Making Center. Parsons Making Center is a collection of more than 70,000 sq. ft. of labs, shops, studios, and open workspaces that provide curricular support for making across a broad range of mediums and disciplines and supports experimentation and interdisciplinary collaboration.  The student assistant should be a personable, proactive, detail-oriented individual who will become integral to the daily workings of the facilities within the Making Center, with the ability to learn new skills and technologies as needed.  Duties entail assisting students and faculty with the checkout of tools/equipment, monitoring making spaces, assisting Managers and Technicians with daily processes and projects, and keeping the facilities clean and orderly.  RESPONSIBILITIES Cultivate a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming learning environment and a respectful shop culture for students, faculty, and staff. Provide a high level of customer service, maintaining a positive and professional demeanor and attitude in all interactions with students, faculty, and staff.  Report for shift on time and review priority tasks with the supervisor  Monitor patrons entering and exiting the shop space and be ready and available to assist them  Provide information to students, faculty, staff, and the general public regarding department services, policies, and procedures Perform basic reception duties including greeting visitors and answering phone calls professionally and courteously  Assist students and faculty with reservations and equipment requests  Assist Making Center Staff with shop upkeep, organization, and maintenance including:  Student Film Office Techs: Support Film Office managers with Film Office duties by maintaining film equipment and resources Assist  faculty and students with equipment.  Work with additional online resources including (websites, web-based platforms  Assist with on-site check ins and checkouts of camera and grip equipment Student Classroom Student Assistants: Attend all class or assigned workshops sessions- Classroom Technicians will have to arrive early to checkout equipment, and stay to the end of class to pack and return equipment. support faculty and students in use of Film Office equipment.  Perform tasks to assist in the maintenance, troubleshooting, and repair of various machinery  Perform regular upkeep of shops and spaces to maintain organization and cleanliness  Complete special projects as assigned  Participate in training sessions and staff meetings  MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Must be an active continuing matriculated student Excellent interpersonal, oral and written communication skills, close attention to detail, and strong organizational and time management abilities. Able to understand and follow verbal and written instructions from supervisor and communicate clearly with Making Center users Adaptable and consistent when notifying the supervisor of schedule changes Attention to detail Ability to interact with students, faculty, and staff of diverse backgrounds Ability to work without close supervision or alone Familiarity with Google Suite (Calendar, Gmail, Docs, Sheets, etc.) Ability to lift items up to 25lbs Ability to work non-traditional hours such as evenings and weekends WORK MODE On-Campus Position  -  Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI Hourly Rate:   $17.00hr/hr We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Provided customer service and front-desk support in a diverse and inclusive learning environment, assisting students, faculty, and staff with equipment reservations, resource requests, and departmental services. Maintained shop, classroom, and equipment spaces through organization, upkeep, troubleshooting, and equipment management, while supporting daily operations, training sessions, and special projects. Assisted faculty and students with classroom and Film Office equipment, including check-in/check-out procedures, technical support, and maintaining equipment resources. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/A---66-West-12th-Street/Manager-of-Academic-Planning_JR109314-1": {
      "title": "Manager of Academic Planning",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design and the College of Performing Arts (Mannes, Jazz, and Drama), Lang College and the New School for Social Research, and Parsons Paris . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW Administrative work at Lang/NSSR is collaborative, based on a premise of teamwork, and is student-centered. We are committed in our administrative staff to the same values that undergird Lang and The New School: civic engagement, social justice, and learning. Together we work towards Lang’s success and the success of The New School. In this spirit, there is a tradition of contributing creatively and generously both within the focus areas of one’s position and as needed and available in other areas. The Manager of Academic Planning supports curriculum building for the Eugene Lang College of Liberal Arts (Lang) and The New School for Social Research (NSSR) within the Academic Planning and Curriculum Hub. The Manager works with the colleges’ academic leadership, faculty, and administrative teams and reports to the Associate Director of Academic Planning. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES   Support the course planning process to ensure the successful implementation of curriculum: Manage and monitor course enrollments throughout the registration process.  Provide strategic recommendations for course additions and cancellations when necessary.  Oversee, track, and efficiently resolve student requests related to course registration; collaborate with Advising with respect to new and continuing student enrollment.  Facilitate communication within programs to inform students, faculty, and staff about curricular developments, policy changes, and registration matters.  Actively engage with the Director of Academic Planning to assure instructional spaces are designed to adequately accommodate courses, including attributes (i.e., software, hardware, furniture, and adjacencies, etc.; serve as point-person on room scheduling matters for academic programs.  Work in concert with Associate Dean of Part-Time Faculty Affairs and Associate Dean of Administrative Faculty Affairs to assure part-time faculty obligations are realized for schools; support processes to identify need for and proper placement of Teaching Assistants and Teaching Fellows; assure placement for Full-Time Faculty.  Supervise and provide ongoing oversight in the production, completion, submission, proofing and revising of key documentation for classes in the fall, spring and summer semesters.  Create and maintain shared schedule documentation containing information including, but not limited to, overall curricular program offerings, faculty assignments, course meeting days and times, and room assignments.  Create and maintain shared curricular documentation containing information including, but not limited to, course pedagogy, course descriptions, co- and prerequisite information, room-type preferences, adjacencies, seat reservations, and course restrictions.  Provide regular college-wide curricular data reports that highlight key factors such as enrollment trends, cross registration, faculty and space utilization, and other reports as requested. Support part-time faculty (PTF) affairs to facilitate compliance with UAW-ACT Local 7902 collective bargaining agreement and academic planning processes: Manage and update PTF data needed for overall academic planning cycle.  Develop and complete PTF reports necessary for both college-wide curriculum planning purposes and those requested by central University offices. Perform additional tasks as required in support of the Academic Planning and Curriculum Hub and the overall operations of the College.  MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s Degree with related experience. Minimum of 5 years of experience in higher education or a related field. Demonstrated ability to analyze, summarize, and draw conclusions from large datasets. High level of computer proficiency in Google Drive, MS Office, and online database systems; strong knowledge of word-processing, spreadsheet, and database software is essential Ability to work well under pressure, take initiative, and follow through on multiple tasks while maintaining a high degree of accuracy, speed and poise. Ability to communicate well with different populations at the University including faculty, students, and staff. Excellent task-management, organizational, and inter-personal/service skills. Ability to problem solve and take initiative.  Commitment to discretion when working with private and protected data.  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree. Knowledge of and proficiency in Banner, Tableau, Degreeworks, and WorkDay and the ability to pull and prepare reports out of these systems. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Hybrid work arrangements may be considered on a case-by-case basis, depending on the nature of the role and operational needs. Any such arrangement must be discussed and approved in advance by the appropriate division lead or their designee. #LI-ONSITE SALARY RANGE $70,000 - $73,000 per annum WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. BENEFITS AT THE NEW SCHOOL The New School is committed to supporting the well-being and success of our faculty and staff. We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their eligible dependents. Highlights include: Health & Wellness Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Financial Wellness   Retirement plan administered by TIAA Qualified Transportation Expense Plan Work-Life Balance Paid vacation and sick leave, with accruals starting on your first day Paid holidays and floating holidays Workmode & Telework Policy (if applicable) Professional Growth Career advancement and professional development opportunities Access to university programs, lectures, and events featuring world-renowned speakers and organizations Tuition waiver benefit for eligible employees and dependents Additional Perks Employee discounts with local vendors and service providers We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Course-Assistant-for-Parsons-Fall-Academy--Grades-3-12-_JR109342": {
      "title": "Course Assistant for Parsons Fall Academy (Grades 3-12)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-27\nPosted: Posted 9 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJoin The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to approximately  9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design and the College of Performing Arts (Mannes, Jazz, and Drama), Lang College and the New School for Social Research, and Parsons Paris . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. Parsons Academy offers a variety of art and design courses for students in grades 3 through 12 in subjects ranging from fine arts and illustration to design disciplines such as fashion design, interior design, photography, animation, and more. Students in grades 9-12 with prior art and design experiences may take our portfolio development course to re-envision their current body of creative work as they create portfolio presentations for the college admissions process. Classes meet on campus on Saturdays in the spring semester. This position will assist with teaching and learning in a class environment for students ranging from Grades 3-12 through non-instructional activities. The Course Assistant reports to the Assistant Director of Operations and Planning, Parsons Academy. This position is expected to work on campus on the following days. The work schedule will be finalized upon hiring. October 3 - December 12, 2026 Saturdays (except Thanksgiving holiday - No classes on Saturday, November 28) 10:00 am-1:00 pm ET (3 hours of paid time) This position is covered by a collective bargaining agreement between SENS-UAW, Local 7902, and the University. RESPONSIBILITIES Attending class sessions and supporting faculty, including chaperoning for field trips. Assisting with classroom set-up and breakdown, including for Open Studios.  Demonstrating techniques. Collecting assignments and projects. Building community among students to serve academic success. Assisting new students with campus navigation. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Current New School students in good academic standing and enrolled for Fall 2026. Responsible and punctual with the ability to meet deadlines and respond promptly. Positive disposition to represent the university and a willingness to help students from diverse backgrounds progress in their summer intensive experience. Proficiency with Adobe Creative Suite. Proficiency with Canvas. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with art and design. Flexibility and willingness to support the New School community. WORK MODE On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $25.13 per hour We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Parsons Academy Course Assistant offers assistance in teaching and learning in an art and design class environment for students ranging from Grades 3-12 through non-instructional activities, which include supporting faculty, chaperoning field trips, assisting with classroom set-up and breakdown, demonstrating techniques and collecting assignments and projects. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/A---66-West-12th-Street/Manager-of-Faculty-Affairs_JR109311-1": {
      "title": "Manager of Faculty Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin The New School   At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design and the College of Performing Arts (Mannes, Jazz, and Drama), Lang College/New School for Social Research, and Parsons Paris . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW Administrative work at Lang/NSSR is collaborative, based on a premise of teamwork, and is student-centered. We are committed in our administrative staff to the same values that undergird Lang and The New School: civic engagement, social justice, and learning. Together we work towards Lang’s success and the success of The New School. In this spirit, there is a tradition of contributing creatively and generously both within the focus areas of one’s position and as needed and available in other areas. The Manager of Faculty Affairs supports the work of the Faculty Affairs Hub at Lang/NSSR.. The Faculty Affairs Hub supports the administration of both Full-time Faculty (FTF), Part-time Faculty (PTF), and Teaching Fellows (TF) as well as compliance with the Full-time Faculty handbook, UAW PTF and ASW SENS union contracts. The position reports to the Associate Dean of Administrative Faculty Affairs and will also support and have a dotted line to the Assistant Dean of Part-time Faculty Affairs.   CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Faculty Review and Compliance Coordinate and support confidential review processes for full-time faculty reappointment, tenure, promotion, and annual evaluation as needed (in conjunction with the Assistant Dean of Faculty Affairs). Organize records tracking upcoming reappointment and promotion reviews in coordination with the provost’s office. Manage information packets for faculty designees supporting faculty reviews. Manage final faculty review materials in preparation for school-based reappointment and promotion review committees. Manage distribution of dossiers, course evaluations, external and department letters, deans’ letters, and final dockets. In coordination with the Assistant Dean, develop and distribute general academic policies for faculty, including central guidelines on syllabi requirements, attendance, and grading; remain well-versed in faculty academic policies. Hiring, Recruitment, and Visiting Scholars Oversee completion from start to finish faculty hiring processes. This includes: managing search postings and informing departments about general search guidelines; drafting faculty contracts for review by deans and provosts once contract negotiations are complete; and managing all HR processes with faculty to formally complete hiring needs. Support faculty search and recruitment, including Heuss professors, ensuring jobs are accurately posted, archiving application materials, supporting search committees, and visiting scholar paperwork and tracking as needed. Direct the school’s Visiting Scholars program, explaining procedures and visa needs. Work with department chairs and secretaries to implement the program successfully, and hire and train part-time support staff on policies, in-take, letters of invitation, and program file management. Hire and oversee Teaching Fellow and Teaching Assistant appointments, in accordance with the SENS-UAW CBA. Administrative, Data, and Financial Support Oversee time-sensitive visa requests for school faculty and term visitors; work independently on visa paperwork with internal and external legal specialists and the office of international scholars. Maintain oversight of Memorandums of Understanding (MOUs) outlining additional faculty compensation, and coordinate payments with the Senior Budget Director. Serve as the point person for tracking FTF/TF absences/safe and sick hours and writing MOUs for substitution payments (in conjunction with the Assistant Dean of Faculty Affairs). Manage tracking records on full-time faculty workload, academic leave accrual, and leave requests. Ensure final sabbatical approvals are accurately transmitted to the budget director and placed into HR systems in a timely fashion. Construct and manage input of faculty data over time (e.g., school-based charts on faculty status, leaves, MOUs, and service assignments); serve as MyDay partner maintaining centralized full-time faculty information. Assist with updating academic appointments in MyDay as needed. General Faculty Affairs Support Work with the Assistant Deans to support faculty orientations, workshops, programs, and other initiatives; update the faculty packet. Track data on missing or late grades and follow-up with faculty as needed. Serve as the liaison for EvaluationKit, including requesting updated access for chairs/directors, reviewing course evaluation configuration each term, and updating TF/TA information in Banner for course evaluations. Prepare and maintain various faculty data sets for the Assistant Deans with an emphasis on data accuracy, integrity, and confidentiality. Perform other administrative duties as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor’s degree with related professional experience. At least three years’ work experience in educational administration. Self-starter capable of managing multiple responsibilities in a complex work environment. Ability to work successfully independently as well as part of a team. Ability to communicate well with diverse populations including faculty and staff throughout the University. Excellent written, analytical, and communication skills with a high level of professionalism and discretion.  Proficiency in Microsoft Office applications and Google docs Experience working with data and generating reports. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Master’s degree. Knowledge of Banner, Tableau, and WorkDay and the ability to pull and prepare reports out of these systems. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Hybrid work arrangements may be considered on a case-by-case basis, depending on the nature of the role and operational needs. Any such arrangement must be discussed and approved in advance by the appropriate division lead or their designee. #LI-ONSITE SALARY RANGE $70,000 - $73,000 per annum WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. BENEFITS AT THE NEW SCHOOL The New School is committed to supporting the well-being and success of our faculty and staff. We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their eligible dependents. Highlights include: Health & Wellness Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Financial Wellness  Retirement plan administered by TIAA Qualified Transportation Expense Plan Work-Life Balance Paid vacation and sick leave, with accruals starting on your first day Paid holidays and floating holidays Workmode & Telework Policy (if applicable) Professional Growth Career advancement and professional development opportunities Access to university programs, lectures, and events featuring world-renowned speakers and organizations Tuition waiver benefit for eligible employees and dependents Additional Perks Employee discounts with local vendors and service providers We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/U---63-Fifth-Avenue/Assistant-Director-for-Research-and-Instruction_JR109291-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Director for Research and Instruction",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-26\nPosted: Posted 10 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to approximately 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design and the College of Performing Arts (Mannes, Jazz, and Drama), Lang College and the New School for Social Research, and Parsons Paris . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. Reporting to the Director of Research & Instructional Services (RIS), the Assistant Director provides leadership in the planning, management, assessment, and strategic development of research and instructional services. Position duties are concentrated in supporting departmental assessment and analytics, developing and advancing strategic initiatives, and serving as liaison in subject areas related to management and entrepreneurship. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Assistant Director of Research & Instructional Services is a key member of the department's leadership team, balancing operational leadership with opportunities to strengthen and evolve library services in response to the changing needs of the university community. Working collaboratively with library colleagues, faculty, and academic programs, the Assistant Director supervises the Research Unit, leads assessment efforts that inform decision-making, and helps identify and implement new initiatives, including emerging areas such as scholarly communication. The successful candidate will bring strong leadership, analytical thinking, and a collaborative approach to enhancing research, teaching, and learning while contributing to the Libraries' long-term goals. This is a full-time position.   CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Supervisory Duties Supervise Research & Instructional Services in the absence of the Director. Supervise assigned Subject Librarians.  Lead “Research Unit” and oversee areas of focus: Assessment and analytics Data visualization Scholarly communication and open publishing Assessment Duties Make budget recommendations for collection management. Ensure processes are effective, regularly assessing services and recommending revisions.  Develop assessment strategies and actively participate in the implementation of strategic planning and goals.  Generate and analyze departmental statistics, incorporating data visualization tools. Operational Duties Jointly oversee and carry out research and instructional services (in-person, by phone and virtually) for library locations.  Serve as liaison for programs within management and entrepreneurship (e.g., Fashion Communication, Fashion Management, and Media Management) by providing: outreach, instruction, research assistance, reserves and new program support, collection development, online guides and tutorials.  Develop and coordinate services that support scholarly communication, including open publishing, and provide guidance to faculty and researchers on evolving publishing practices. Support the development and assessment of new services, resources, and initiatives that enhance research, teaching, and library services. Collaboration Duties Partner with other library units to ensure excellent internal/external customer service standards. Collaborate with faculty, academic programs, and library colleagues to advance teaching, learning, and equitable access to library-supported course materials. Cultivate partnerships across the Libraries and the New School community to identify and advance scholarly communication initiatives and other emerging services. Participate in local and national forums in order to stay current with trends regarding research and instruction services in academic libraries. Participate in working groups, e.g., Stats and Analytics. Other duties as required.  QUALIFICATIONS Relevant Bachelor’s degree from a four-year program. ALA-­accredited MLS. Strong understanding of research data management, statistical analysis, scholarly publishing and open access. Supervisory and/or project management experience. Excellent interpersonal, written, and oral communication skills.  Ability to thrive in constantly evolving environment and eager to facilitate innovative change.  Ability to manage multiple priorities and meet deadlines. 3+ years experience in an academic library environment. Master’s in relevant subject area. Exemplary teaching skills or training experience. Demonstrated knowledge of current technologies related to research and instruction. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-ONSITE SALARY RANGE $77,000 - 80,000 per annum WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. BENEFITS AT THE NEW SCHOOL The New School is committed to supporting the well-being and success of our faculty and staff. We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their eligible dependents. Highlights include: Health & Wellness Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Financial Wellness   Retirement plan administered by TIAA Qualified Transportation Expense Plan Work-Life Balance Paid vacation and sick leave, with accruals starting on your first day Paid holidays and floating holidays Workmode & Telework Policy (if applicable) Professional Growth Career advancement and professional development opportunities Access to university programs, lectures, and events featuring world-renowned speakers and organizations Tuition waiver benefit for eligible employees and dependents Additional Perks Employee discounts with local vendors and service providers We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Discovery-Systems-and-Electronic-Resources-Specialist_JR109312-1": {
      "title": "Discovery Systems and Electronic Resources Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin The New School   At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 8,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang College of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW   Reporting to the Assistant Director for Library Systems, the Discovery Systems and Electronic Resources Specialist supports the discovery and access of the library’s resources. The position provides support for electronic resource troubleshooting and discovery services. This role works closely with other Digital Library and Technical Services teams (Acquisitions, Metadata, and Collection Services) and consults with public services teams to enhance how users find, access, evaluate, and use library, archives, and special collections resources within the primary library catalog and related applications. The position supports the technology that connects faculty and students with library materials. The position requires strong analytical judgment, systems thinking, documentation skills, and the ability to translate access problems, metadata issues, usage data, and user behavior into practical service improvements. Work will directly contribute to resolving access and discovery challenges, making a meaningful difference for library users on all global New School campuses. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Primary Responsibilities Discovery & Electronic Resource Support Monitor and analyze catalog and electronic resource usage Troubleshoot electronic resource access (OpenAthens) and metadata issues  Recommend and implement discovery and supporting system improvements Coordinate with university, consortial, and vendor support departments Create and review documentation for library staff Facilitate import of new digital collections and secure electronic lending within the discovery interface.  Collaborate with colleagues in the Libraries, Archives, and other areas of the university Enrich and load metadata for electronic/digital library materials in consultation with the Metadata and Collection Services team. Collect, analyze, and present data from various sources Other Duties As Assigned QUALIFICATIONS Required Bachelor’s degree and relevant professional experience, or an equivalent combination of education and experience. Experience supporting electronic resources, discovery systems, metadata workflows, library systems, scholarly communications, or academic information services. Experience with data integrations, APIs, or automated workflows Strong analytical and problem-solving skills   Preferred Master’s degree in Library and Information Science, information management, data analytics, educational technology, publishing, or a related field. Demonstrated experience with Ex Libris Alma/Primo, or comparable library service platforms ( Alma / Primo certification as an example). Experience with Digital Asset Management systems such as ContentDM or Alma-D/Specto Familiarity with specific standards: COUNTER, SUSHI, KBART, and OpenURL Ability to read, adapt, or troubleshoot basic scripts (Python and/or JavaScript), structured data, or configuration files in support of library systems and electronic resource workflows. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement with on-campus library patrons and staff. #LI-Onsite Hybrid work arrangements may be considered on a case-by-case basis, depending on the nature of the role and operational needs. Any such arrangement must be discussed and approved in advance by the appropriate division lead or their designee. SALARY RANGE $66,300 - $70,000 per annum WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. BENEFITS AT THE NEW SCHOOL The New School is committed to supporting the well-being and success of our faculty and staff. We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their eligible dependents. Highlights include: Health & Wellness Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Financial Wellness  Retirement plan administered by TIAA Qualified Transportation Expense Plan Work-Life Balance Paid vacation and sick leave, with accruals starting on your first day Paid holidays and floating holidays Workmode & Telework Policy (if applicable) Professional Growth Career advancement and professional development opportunities Access to university programs, lectures, and events featuring world-renowned speakers and organizations Tuition waiver benefit for eligible employees and dependents Additional Perks Employee discounts with local vendors and service providers We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/JJ---39-West-13th-Street/Student-Assistant-Specialist---Narwhal-Fitness-Instructor---OCSE-_JR109324": {
      "title": "Student Assistant Specialist - Narwhal Fitness Instructor  (OCSE)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Office of Student Engagement oversees community building programs, and seeks a student worker to support programming for commuter students. This position reports to the Associate Director for Recreation & Commuter Engagement. The New School was founded by forward-thinking educators in 1919 to defy the intellectual constraints of a traditional college education.  Reporting to the Associate Director of Recreation, & Commuter Engagement, the Fitness Instructor will be responsible for leading fitness classes, creating content for social media accounts, and acting as the point-person for inquiries and class sign ups. RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as a student fitness instructor during a TNS fitness class.  Create content for the Commuter Group’s NarwhalNation and Instagram pages.  Reply to student inquiries related to the fitness class in question. Lead events in question with a fitness course/lesson plan.  Support students in signing up for the class. Take class attendance per session. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Currently enrolled New School student Demonstrated commitment to community building and teamwork Reliable, organized, and communicative Past fitness experience Ability to lead fitness sessions Able to manage a hybrid schedule with majority in-person hours PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Prior experience/certification working as a fitness instructor is preferred.  WORK MODE Hybrid/Split - Employees hired for this position have regularly scheduled, consistent percentage of time on campus (ex 1-4x/week) and also work some of the time remotely. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE : $19 - $21 / hour We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. ​ SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS * ( if applicable) Questions can be emailed to recreation@newschool.edu but applications must be submitted through the New School WorkDay Jobs Portal for an interview to be scheduled.  Responsibilities: The Fitness Instructor will be responsible for leading fitness classes, creating content for social media accounts, and acting as the point-person for inquiries and class sign ups. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/JJ---39-West-13th-Street/Graduate-Mentor----Career-Pathways-Program_JR109206-1": {
      "title": "Graduate Mentor -- Career Pathways Program",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Center for Career Design and Development seeks graduate student mentors for their Career Pathways Mentoring Program Student Assistant Specialist. The Career Pathways Mentoring Program pairs a Graduate Mentor with four undergraduate students to help support their academic and professional aspirations. Mentorship is expected to help undergraduate students understand the value of finishing their degrees as a path to a career. We strongly encourage graduate students from across The New School to apply. RESPONSIBILITIES Available to meet with mentees — 4 meetings per month (in person or remote) The first meeting with mentee must be in person Available to attend in person and support two group meetings over a catered lunch, one at the beginning of the program and one at the end Responsible for encouraging your mentee and offering guidance as appropriate; steering mentee to university resources as needed; communicating concerns with pilot program co chairs as necessary Participation in an 8-Hour Asynchronous Peer Mentoring Certificate program will be required (provided) prior to the start of the semester. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Graduate student in good standing Completion of at least one semester of full time study Graduation date no earlier than May 2026 GPA equal to 3.5 or higher Approachable, friendly, supportive, desire to and able to provide guidance Knowledge of university resources WORK MODE Hybrid/Split – Employees hired for this position have regularly scheduled, consistent percentage of time on campus (ex 1-4x/week) and also work some of the time remotely. #LI-DNI Hourly Rate: $21.00 per hour; 5 hours per week Fall and Spring Semesters SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS * ( if applicable) Application Materials ● Résumé or CV ● Cover Letter that explains in your own words why you would make a good mentor to undergraduate students We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Graduate Mentor is paired with four undergraduate students to help support their academic and professional aspirations. Mentorship is expected to help undergraduate students understand the value of finishing their degrees as a path to a career. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/U---63-Fifth-Avenue/Assistant-Manager-of-Mechanics--Sewing-and-Soft-Construction-Fixed-Term_JR109216-1": {
      "title": "Assistant Manager of Mechanics, Sewing and Soft Construction Fixed-Term",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 11 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJoin The New School At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang College of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Parsons School of Design, a division of The New School, invites applications for the position of Assistant Manager of Mechanics, Sewing & Soft Construction within the Making Center. The Parsons Making Center encompasses over 70,000 square feet of laboratories, shops, and studios that foster experimentation and interdisciplinary collaboration. This role is responsible for the operational management of the Sewing facilities and equipment, ensuring a safe, healthy environment for undergrad, graduate, and continuing education students and faculty while overseeing essential administrative duties. We seek a personable, proactive, and detail-oriented professional to support a wide range of processes in sewing and soft construction, with a core focus on repair and maintenance of machinery.  This is an exempt administrative position reporting to the Facilities Manager of Sewing and Soft Construction, Making Center, based in a fast-paced environment that operates year-round. The hire is for a 3-year fixed term subject to end unless otherwise approved for renewal.   CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Maintain a clean and safe working environment and uphold a respectful shop culture for students, faculty, and staff. Lead the process to troubleshoot, repair, maintain, install, and ensure continuous operation and support for a variety of industrial and domestic sewing equipment. Lead the efforts and train other staff on routine maintenance of equipment, in addition to developing Standard Operating Procedures and preventative maintenance schedules. Assist supervisor and Making Center Leadership with the following: Assist faculty and students. Lead demo sessions about various pieces of equipment. Make hardware/software purchase and process recommendations. Create web page content. Create and conduct orientations, trainings, and tours. Participate in the onboarding process for new technician staff through peer-to-peer trainings and skills sharing. Maintain administrative systems for scheduling, record-keeping, inventories, and metrics tracking. Provide support for store and tool checkout functions as related to assigned areas Oversee daily workings of the Making Center facilities as assigned. Supervise student workers, including training, tracking accountability, and assigning tasks during shifts. Oversee tool and equipment checkout for both in-shop/lab use and off-site special requests. Create clear, accurate, user-friendly technical documentation, signage, and instructions for labs and equipment. Assist with facility improvement projects and special Making Center, program, school or Parsons-wide initiatives as needed. Adapt to changes in the work environment; adjust approach and prioritize competing demands as necessary. Provide a high level of customer service, maintaining a positive and professional demeanor and attitude in all interactions with students, faculty, and staff.  Cultivate a diverse, inclusive, and welcoming learning environment with productive and positive workplace relationships. Stay current with relevant technology and developments within the field. Attend regularly scheduled Making Center staff meetings and perform other duties as assigned by supervisor. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS A Bachelor’s Degree and/or 3 years of relevant or professional experience within the industry. Flexible schedule - ability to work non-traditional schedules that may include nights and weekends, in addition to scheduling shifts with semester changes. Completion of university required staff trainings and necessary COF's for all Making Center Facilities within the first 6 months of employment. Become proficient in WebCheckout or current equipment management system within the first 6 months of employment. Knowledge of industrial sewing and soft construction techniques, finishing, and troubleshooting for traditional garment and accessory construction, as well as experimental projects. Technical knowledge of a variety of industrial sewing techniques and machinery, as well as experience with repair and maintenance of equipment Expertise in threading, safe operation, and routine maintenance of sewing machines. Ability to identify machine issues, troubleshoot, and conduct repairs to keep 400+ machines in working order.  Facilitate repairs with external vendors as needed, including procurement and contract management.  Understanding of working in a cross-platform (Windows and macOS) environment. Familiarity with Adobe Creative Cloud and Google Suite. Excellent interpersonal, oral, and written communication skills, close attention to detail, and strong organizational and time management abilities. Strong ability to assist students working in an interdisciplinary and/or experimental manner from concept to fabrication. A desire to learn new skills and processes related to Parsons Making Center initiatives. Ability to handle objects weighing up to 25 lbs and on occasion may be expected to lift objects weighing up to 50 lbs  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Trained sewing mechanic. Expansive technical experience servicing specialized industrial sewing machinery such as lockstitch, overlock, coverstitch, flatlock, post, walking foot, blind hem, chainstitch, embroidery, sonobond, and skiver machines. Experience with shoe-making processes, leatherwork, and fiber art practices. Experience with building and hand tools to maintain all studio equipment and furniture.  Knowledge of Webcheckout or comparable equipment management systems.  Experience with large-scale hardware and software deployments. Experience with Juki, Consew, Brother, and Singer sewing machinery.   WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-ONSITE SALARY RANGE $66,300 - $69,000 per year WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. BENEFITS AT THE NEW SCHOOL The New School is committed to supporting the well-being and success of our faculty and staff. We offer a comprehensive benefits package designed to meet the diverse needs of our employees and their eligible dependents. Highlights include: Health & Wellness Comprehensive medical, dental, and vision coverage Employee Assistance Program (EAP) Financial Wellness  Retirement plan administered by TIAA Qualified Transportation Expense Plan Work-Life Balance Paid vacation and sick leave, with accruals starting on your first day Paid holidays and floating holidays Workmode & Telework Policy (if applicable) Professional Growth Career advancement and professional development opportunities Access to university programs, lectures, and events featuring world-renowned speakers and organizations Tuition waiver benefit for eligible employees and dependents Additional Perks Employee discounts with local vendors and service providers We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS  Interview finalists will be asked to come in for an in-person interview in which their technical skills will be assessed.  We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Mannes-Opera--Student-Assistant---FWS_JR109358": {
      "title": "Mannes Opera, Student Assistant - FWS",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nINTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH The Mannes School of Music at the College of Performing Arts seeks a highly motivated student to serve as Mannes Opera, Student Assistant. We’re looking for an engaging, vibrant, and personable individual to support initiatives within the Mannes Opera Department. This position reports to the Managing Artistic Director of Mannes Opera, and is an ideal position for students who are interested in a career in opera, and performing arts or non-profit management. This position is open to student applicants with Federal Work Study awards. RESPONSIBILITIES Collate content and produce programs for shows and events Manage various media accounts, curating the alumni newsletter and weekly social media postings Assist planning of master classes, workshops, and other events - providing on-site presence as needed Support the organization and management of the Opera Con event Assist with score distribution, retrieval, and storage before and after rehearsals and performances Liaise with Mannes Opera guest artists and other artistic personnel, serving as an onsite departmental contact Additional responsibilities as assigned MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Knowledge of theater/opera productions and repertoire Capability to work independently, or collaboratively on a team Background and education in the performing arts Comfort/experience with Google Suite applications (Docs, Sheets, Forms, etc.) Strong social media skills Recipient of Federal Work Study award PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Current student in a College of Performing Arts degree program Prior administrative and/or event planning experience WORK MODE : On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE: $17.00 Hours per Week: 4-10 We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS * ( if applicable) Applicants should submit a resume and cover letter outlining their skills and experience concerning this position; and their Federal Work Study award letter if applicable. Responsibilities: Manage departmental communications and content creation by producing show programs, curating the alumni newsletter, and overseeing weekly social media channels. Provide key operational and logistical support for Mannes Opera productions and events through score management, event planning, and serving as the primary on-site contact for guest artists. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/FWS---Front-of-House-Usher--Student-Assistant_JR109365": {
      "title": "FWS - Front of House Usher, Student Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Front of House area at the College of Performing Arts seeks a highly motivated student to serve as an Usher. We’re looking for responsible, personable, communicative, and punctual individuals to support initiatives within the Front of House area. This position reports to the Manager of Event Operations and is an ideal position for students who are interested in a career in the performing arts, events, and production. This position is open to student applicants with Federal Work Study awards. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Greet patrons and answer questions Distribute printed programs to patrons Assist patrons in finding their seats Check in patrons using our app-based check-in system Execute stage changes for classical recitals when assigned Additional responsibilities as assigned QUALIFICATIONS Background and education in the performing arts PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS  2 years usher experience 2 years experience in customer service Recipient of Federal Work Study award WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE: $17.00 Hours per Week: 3-20, or as needed. Not to exceed 20 hours in a single workweek while classes are in session. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit both a resume and cover letter outlining their interest, skills, and experience pertaining to this position; and a Federal Work Study award letter if applicable. Responsibilities: Provide front-of-house support by greeting patrons, processing app-based check-ins, distributing programs, and assisting guests with seating and inquiries. Execute stage changes for classical recitals and perform additional operational responsibilities as assigned. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Front-of-House-Usher--Student-Assistant_JR109364": {
      "title": "Front of House Usher, Student Assistant",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-24\nPosted: Posted 12 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Front of House area at the College of Performing Arts seeks a highly motivated student to serve as an Usher. We’re looking for responsible, personable, communicative, and punctual individuals to support initiatives within the Front of House area. This position reports to the Manager of Event Operations and is an ideal position for students who are interested in a career in the performing arts, events, and production. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Greet patrons and answer questions Distribute printed programs to patrons Assist patrons in finding their seats Check in patrons using our app-based check-in system Execute stage changes for classical recitals when assigned Additional responsibilities as assigned QUALIFICATIONS Background and education in the performing arts PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS  2 years usher experience 2 years experience in customer service WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-DNI Hourly Rate: $17.00 Hours per Week: 3-20, or as needed. Not to exceed 20 hours in a single workweek while classes are in session. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit both a resume and cover letter outlining their interest, skills, and experience pertaining to this position; and a Federal Work Study award letter if applicable. Responsibilities: Provide front-of-house support by greeting patrons, processing app-based check-ins, distributing programs, and assisting guests with seating and inquiries. Execute stage changes for classical recitals and perform additional operational responsibilities as assigned. We look forward to receiving your application!"
