      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nRESPONSIBILITIES Student tutor will assist other students in out-of-class by tutoring and answering questions about course content taught in class. Creating a weekly schedule where students can sign up and reserve time to work one on one with tutor.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Interest and Knowledge : Strong interest in systems and ID, AD, PD software. Completed first year of SCE course work.  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Interest and Knowledge : Strong interest in systems and ID, AD, PD software. Completed first year of SCE course work.  WORK MODE: In person #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE : $29.20/hour We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.   This position is covered by a collective bargaining agreement between SENS-UAW, Local 7902 and the University. Responsibilities: Working with students outside the classroom that have specific needs around key SCE software. Tutors will be responsible for c reating a weekly schedule where students can sign up and reserve time to work one on one with tutor.   We look forward to receiving your application!"
