      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-10\nPosted: Posted 26 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nINTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH The School of Drama at the College of Performing Arts seeks a highly motivated student to serve as Drama/Bank Street Programs, Student Assistant. We’re looking for an organized and enthusiastic individual with a self-starter disposition interested in all aspects of drama production & operations to support the School of Drama’s programs at 151 Bank Street . This is an ideal position for students who are interested in a career in non-profit, performing arts, or higher education administration.. This position is open to student applicants with Federal Work Study awards. RESPONSIBILITIES Support daily operations within the School of Drama and Production programs with scheduling, paperwork, database upkeep, and general organizational/operational tasks Station Bank Street’s Welcome Hub in Room 102 to answer student, faculty and visitor questions Assist with faculty copy/IT needs, mail distribution, stocking supplies, program printing, special events, and mainstage marketing support.  Generate information and update College of Performing Arts Calendar; Post monthly on Call Board Support needs for classes / small projects Manage supply orders and restocking (tape, first aid, etc.) Create and circulate materials for the Arts Letters Maintain photo archives, scripts and production books Maintain physical supplies in Bank Street as requested Additional responsibilities as assigned MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Recipient of a Federal Work Study award. Ability to commit to a consistent weekly schedule. Excellent written and verbal communication, attention to detail, and group and independent problem solving skills Working knowledge of Google Suite: Drive, Calendar, etc General knowledge of theater practices and protocols Commitment to diversity and inclusion PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Current student in a College of Performing Arts degree program At least one semester at The New 