uple of homework exercises. Tutors can assist students in their written and oral assignments, mini-projects and exam material review. ● Assist students in the oral and written language used for class presentations providing corrections if needed and constructive feedback. ● Facilitate interactive speaking and listening exercises to build a real-world conversation skill. ● Contact language professors to participate in cultural class events allowing students to integrate in foreign language culture customs and social conventions. ● Set up their STARFISH office hours according to the university academic calendar and remove it during holidays. Tutoring is only offer at the university. ● Submit their online timesheets for payment through My-Day application. ● Communicate immediately when a tutoring session has been cancelled. Contact the student and the program coordinator to inform about it. ● Inform the tutoring coordinator if students are not at tending sessions. Tutoring is a free service and if a student does not attend the session their tutoring privilege can be removed. ● Register all sessions performed in the tutoring excel track sheet provided every semester, indicating the day and time the session was performed and the student name too. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS ● The tutoring job position is opened to students that are currently enrolled at the New School University only. ● Native or near native fluency in the target language is desired, alongside strong English communication skills to clearly explain complex language rules. ● Experience as a prior tutor in high school or other institutions in the country or abroad is a plus. ● Strong and interpersonal skills such as patience, empathy, respect and tolerance to students diverse opinions. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Applicants with advanced knowledge of literature, grammar, writing and speaking in the target language is a plus. WORK MODE Hybrid - Employees hired for this position primarily work remotely with the occasional on- campus presence required with advanced notice. Employees in this role will also be expected to use their best judgment to be on campus, when necessary, in order to best fulfill the responsibilities of their job descriptions. #LI-DNI Hourly Rate: $29.20 We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. This position is covered by a collective bargaining agreement between SENS-UAW, Local 7902 and the University. Responsibilities: The Language Tutor provides one-on-one tutoring to help students strengthen their language skills, including grammar, pronunciation, homework, presentations, and written and oral assignments. Tutors complete required training, promote tutoring services, maintain accurate records, and support cultural engagement activities. They report to the faculty tutoring coordinator and must be currently enrolled students with strong language proficiency and communication skills. We look forward to receiving your application!"
