    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Part-Time-Faculty---Parsons-School-of-Design_JR109030": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty | Parsons School of Design",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-07-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School , a university known for its progressive approach to education, comprises seven outstanding Divisions bound by a common purpose: To educate and inspire undergraduate, graduate, and adult learners to make significant contributions to their own fields and to the world at large. Located in historic Greenwich Village, the New School launches the careers of world citizens whose ideas, innovations, and accomplishments forge new paths in design, humanities, public policy, the social sciences, and the performing arts. RESPONSIBILITIES Parsons School of Design  at The New School is accepting applications for possible Part-Time Faculty positions in all five design schools for upcoming semesters. Class times may be evenings and/or weekends. Duties may include the following: Teaching graduate and/or undergraduate students within a defined field of expertise; Developing and managing course syllabi and ensuring that syllabi meet Program and School standards; Planning and creating lectures, discussions, and course assignments; Assessing student learning outcomes and aiding student success; Submitting grades in a timely manner. Part-time faculty at The New School bargain collectively through Academics Come Together, ACT-UAW, Local 7902. QUALIFICATIONS Vary by disciplinary area, but generally require: A terminal degree in the field of specialty is preferred (MFA, PH.D, ABD, or equivalent); 2-3 years of teaching experience with a variety of teaching methods and curricular perspectives, preferably in a College, University, and/or Art and Design school settings; Ability to work with diverse students and colleagues; Proven success creating inclusive classrooms; Ability to adhere to University COVID-19 Policy and requirements. HOURLY RATE Studio Hourly Rate : $135/contact hr Seminar Hourly Rate : $156/contact hr WORK MODE On-Campus/Online #LI-DNI SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Please prepare a Resume/CV and Cover Letter outlining your previous relevant experience. Please include any relevant portfolio materials and/or a link to your professional website if applicable. The New School is an equal opportunity employer and does not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application! We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/HML-Part-Time-Program-Administrator_JR108963": {
      "title": "HML Part Time Program Administrator",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nParsons the New School for Design seeks a responsible, detail-oriented Part-Time Program Administrator to provide administrative support to Healthy Materials Lab Directors and staff on grant-related activities that are 100% effort (21hrs/week). This role is supported by funds from Friends of Healthy Materials Initiative. This position provides a flexible work schedule with a high expectation of reliability. Must be available to work at least three days a week. This is a fixed term, part-time position for 21 hours a week and will be benefit-eligible. HML Related Activities ( 100% effort)   Work in the Lab is fast-paced and complex and applicants should be able and willing to multi-task. The candidate must possess strong organizational and communication skills including excellent writing skills. They must be punctual, logical, and self-sufficient and possess a high level of technical computer literacy. This position provides a flexible work schedule with a high expectation of reliability. This is a union administrative position governed by a collective bargaining agreement between Local 1205 Teamsters and the University. The New School is strongly committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace and particularly seeks applications from members of underrepresented groups, as well as candidates who share this commitment.   Responsibilities: Oversight and coordination of public programs, private events, and internal/external meetings. Includes adjusting work schedule on days with evening events. Schedule HML communications, media promotion, and public relations, including mailing list maintenance and upkeep. Undertake writing projects to disseminate the work of the Lab. Assist in updating students through Canvas and/or distributing a range of digital communications for HML’s eLearning programs. Administration of academic partnerships including project management. Creation, implementation, and management of program-level communications and calendar. Oversee expense tracking and reconciliation, and coordinate with relevant university offices as needed. Qualifications :  Bachelor’s Degree with equivalent experience required. Exceptionally professional and proactive with an interest in Material Health. Highly organized and detail-oriented. Demonstrated ability to prioritize, problem-solve, manage diverse activities, and meet deadlines. Exceptional communication, interpersonal, and collaboration skills. Pleasant demeanor and positive, can-do attitude. Work mode: This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Hybrid work arrangements may be considered on a case-by-case basis, depending on the nature of the role and operational needs. Any such arrangement must be discussed and approved in advance by the appropriate division lead or their designee. #LI-Onsite Hourly Range: $32.98/hr - $36.42     We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/FWS-Student-Assistant---Financial-Aid_JR108971": {
      "title": "FWS Student Assistant - Financial Aid",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nReporting to the Associate Director of Financial Aid, the Federal Work-Study Student Assistants will work collaboratively with other colleagues within Enrollment Management to guide students and their families through the financial aid application process and their status regarding financial aid. The Financial Aid Student Assistant will act as a first responder for the financial aid office, providing welcoming, courteous, prompt, and accurate information, as well as providing support with data collection, research, and reporting. Students in this position must have received a Federal Work Study award. Responsibilities: ● Respond to phone calls & emails from prospective/returning students and their families, providing friendly, accurate, and timely information about their financial aid ● Develop knowledge of the different colleges within the new school, degree programs, and majors ● Assist students with the application process, providing information on application deadlines and requirements ●Escalate calls and email inquiries appropriately ●Provide prospective/returning students and families with Financial Aid information ●Assist newly/returning admitted students and appropriately triage inquiries within the FA department and to other university departments (admissions, student accounts, registrar, open campus, housing) ●Provide research support on various operations projects ●Light filing, distribution of emails, and forms to financial aid representatives ●Additional projects and ad hoc reports as needed ●Assist in managing our Virtual Zoom Meeting Room and in-person traffic   Qualifications: ● Experience working in a professional office setting ● Customer service and visitor experience are a must ● Interest in higher education and office experience a plus ● Friendly and kind demeanor, attention to detail ● Excellent verbal and written communication skills ● Strong understanding of The New School’s programs ● Familiarity with campus (i.e., offices, computer centers, location of departments, etc.). ● Ability to manage in a diverse population ● Proficiency in Microsoft Word, PowerPoint, and Excel ● An ability to perform multiple tasks ● Must be able to work a minimum of 10-15 hours per week on campus ● This is a Federal Work-Study position. Only apply if you are eligible for Federal Work-Study. Hourly Rate:  $17.00-$19.00 Work Mode:  Hybrid/Split - Employees hired for this position have regularly scheduled, consistent percentage of time on campus and also work some of the time remotely. #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Please Note: This is a Federal Work Study Position for students who were awarded a Federal Work Study (FWS) award, please upload a copy of your FWS Award letter in addition to your other application documents to be considered for this role. Responsibilities: This role assists prospective and returning students with financial aid, application questions, and university resources through phone, email, Zoom, and in-person support. Responsibilities include providing accurate information, directing inquiries to the appropriate departments, and supporting student services. The position also involves administrative tasks, research projects, and other operational support as needed We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Staff-Pianist_JR108967": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Staff Pianist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nINTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Mannes School of Music at The New School’s College of Performing Arts is seeking highly qualified Temporary Overhire Staff Pianists to join its team. Reporting to the Performance and Ensemble Manager, the Overhire Staff Pianists are directly responsible for staff piano services throughout the Mannes School of Music, including performing in students’ lessons, masterclasses, juries, and more. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Mannes School of Music department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Accompany all student performance opportunities, including lessons, masterclasses, classroom activities, annual concerto competition, juries, and more Exhibit professionalism in all interactions with students, faculty, staff, and audience members Respond to inquiries from students, faculty, and staff in a timely manner regarding private lessons, masterclasses, and/or other performance experiences Adhere to departmental guidelines regarding reporting hours, payroll deadlines, and other items Additional responsibilities as requested QUALIFICATIONS Master’s Degree and/or equivalent training in collaborative piano Excellent collaborative piano skills and artistic capabilities Ability to prepare music quickly on an as-needed basis Noted recognition in the collaborative piano field WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-Onsite Hourly Rate: $25.00/hour  WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. The Performance and Ensemble Manager will be in touch in order to schedule an audition with you. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/FWS-Student-Assistant---Parsons-Graduate-Admission_JR108945": {
      "title": "FWS Student Assistant - Parsons Graduate Admission",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-16\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nParsons Student Assistants will work collaboratively in the Parsons Graduate Admission Department responding to and cataloging general inquiries, maintaining digital records, preparing recruitment materials for events, engaging with graduate students in the ZeeMee social app, and performing various administrative tasks. The incumbent will serve as a primary point of contact for inquiries directed to Parsons from internal and external stakeholders. Parsons Student Assistants report directly to an Assistant or Associate Director of Admission.  We are looking for a dynamic, motivated individual who can work independently, but is also a team player. The ideal candidate for this position is a graduate student who is interested in leveraging their own prospective student experience and working on a small team with a focus on fielding inquiries from prospective Parsons Graduate students. Experience in admissions, office administration and customer service is a plus. Applicants must be enrolled in a graduate program at The New School; students from all academic disciplines are encouraged to apply. Strong writing skills are essential. Applicants will be asked to complete a brief writing assignment during the application process. Responsibilities: ●       Monitoring Parsons recruitment inbox inquiries and fielding replies  ●       Drafting email response templates for commonly asked questions ●       Responding to graduate admission inquiries in the ZeeMee social app ●       Provide administrative support to Parsons Admission Directors ●       Assist with admission and recruitment event preparations ●       Additional project-based tasks as needed Minimum Qualifications:  ●       Excellent verbal and written communication skills ●       Proficiency of Microsoft Office Suite and Google Drive ●       Ability to work independently and expediently with limited hands-on supervision ●       Ability to demonstrate discretion in handling confidential applicant information ●       Ability to perform multiple tasks with effective time management and prioritization Preferred Qualifications :  ●       Customer service experience ●       Administrative experience, preferably in a higher education setting   ●       Strong understanding of the Parsons student experience and programming ●       Availability to work 10-15 hours weekly  Hourly Rate : $17/hr Work Mode : Hybrid - Employees hired for this position primarily work remotely with the occasional on-campus presence required with advanced notice. Employees in this role will also be expected to use their best judgment to be on campus when necessary in order to best fulfill the responsibilities of their job descriptions. #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.​ Please Note: This is a Federal Work Study Position for students who were awarded a Federal Work Study (FWS) award, please upload a copy of your FWS Award letter in addition to your other application documents to be considered for this role. Responsibilities: Parsons Student Assistants will work collaboratively in the Parsons Graduate Admission Department responding to and cataloging general inquiries, maintaining digital records, preparing recruitment materials for events, engaging with graduate students in the ZeeMee social app, and performing various administrative tasks. The incumbent will serve as a primary point of contact for inquiries directed to Parsons from internal and external stakeholders. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/B---65-West-11th-Street/Part-Time-Faculty_JR108930": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-08\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School , a university known for its progressive approach to education, its divisions bound by a common purpose: To educate and inspire undergraduate, graduate, and adult learners to make significant contributions to their own fields and to the world at large. Located in historic Greenwich Village, the New School launches the careers of world citizens whose ideas, innovations, and accomplishments forge new paths in design, humanities, public policy, the social sciences, and the performing arts. Eugene Lang College of Liberal Arts at The New School is accepting applications for possible Part-Time Faculty positions. Class times may be evenings and/or weekends. Duties may include the following: Teaching undergraduate students within a defined field of expertise; Developing and managing course syllabi and ensuring that syllabi meet Program and School standards; Planning and creating lectures, discussions, and course assignments; Assessing student learning outcomes and aiding student success; Submitting grades in a timely manner.   QUALIFICATIONS VARY BY DEPARTMENT A terminal degree or equivalent experience in the field of specialty is preferred. 2-3 years of teaching experience with a variety of teaching methods and curricular perspectives, preferably in a College, University, or school setting. Ability to work with diverse students and colleagues; Proven success creating inclusive classrooms; Compensation Studio Hourly Rate: $ 135/contact hr Seminar Hourly Rare: $156/contact hr Work Mode : On Site #LI-DNI Please prepare a Resume/CV and Cover Letter outlining your previous relevant experience. Please include any relevant portfolio materials and/or a link to your professional website if applicable. Part-time faculty at The New School bargain collectively through Academics Come Together, ACT-UAW, Local 7902. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/D---6-East-16th-Street/Part-Time-Faculty_JR108929": {
      "title": "Part-Time Faculty",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School , a university known for its progressive approach to education, its divisions bound by a common purpose: To educate and inspire undergraduate, graduate, and adult learners to make significant contributions to their own fields and to the world at large. Located in historic Greenwich Village, the New School launches the careers of world citizens whose ideas, innovations, and accomplishments forge new paths in design, humanities, public policy, the social sciences, and the performing arts. The New School for Social Research  at The New School is accepting applications for possible Part-Time Faculty positions. Class times may be evenings and/or weekends. Duties may include the following: Teaching graduate  students within a defined field of expertise; Developing and managing course syllabi and ensuring that syllabi meet Program and School standards; Planning and creating lectures, discussions, and course assignments; Assessing student learning outcomes and aiding student success; Submitting grades in a timely manner Part-time faculty at The New School bargain collectively through Academics Come Together, ACT-UAW, Local 7902. QUALIFICATIONS VARY BY DEPARTMENT A terminal degree or equivalent experience in the field of specialty is preferred. 2-3 years of teaching experience with a variety of teaching methods and curricular perspectives, preferably in a College, University, or school setting. Ability to work with diverse students and colleagues; Proven success creating inclusive classrooms; Hourly Rate: STUDIO HOURLY RATE $135/contact hr SEMINAR HOURLY RATE $156/contact hr Work Mode: On Site #LI-DNI Please prepare a Resume/CV and Cover Letter outlining your previous relevant experience. Please include any relevant portfolio materials and/or a link to your professional website if applicable. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.  We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/B---65-West-11th-Street/First-Year-Mentor---Student-Assistant-Specialist_JR108924": {
      "title": "First Year Mentor - Student Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe First Year Mentor program is an exciting leadership opportunity for Lang students to build upon their own academic, pedagogical, and activist work, and to inspire first year students to become part of a community at Lang that values and practices a commitment to care, critical thinking, and social justice. Following a training and orientation in August and early September, First Year Mentors support a group of incoming first year students to help them make a smooth transition to Lang and engage with the campus community.  ​ Responsibilities:    Training involves an intensive introduction to the TNS/Lang campus ecology, offering First Year Mentors an opportunity:  ● Meet with various campus partners from offices, departments, and programs from across the university; ● Learn with and from Lang faculty about best pedagogical practices in and across the liberal arts;  ● Build cohort community and develop a collective programmatic vision for the upcoming academic year; and ● Construct preliminary workshop curricula centered on the connections between social justice, interdisciplinarity, and the liberal arts.   At Orientation, First Year Mentors: ● offer informal support to new first year students and facilitate their arrival onto campus; ● lead an introductory seminar discussion for first year seminar students with first year seminar faculty; ● take first year seminar students on a luncheon walking tour of TNS; and ● lead a panel discussion (“How I Decided”) on major and course selection processes.    Minimum Qualifications:   ·       Completed at least one full semester of coursework at Eugene Lang College ·       In good academic standing   Preferred Qualifications:  ·       Facilitates conversations with ease and interacts respectfully with others ·       Demonstrates (active) listening for understanding and an openness to feedback, learning, and growth ·       Displays effective communication across lines of identity and difference, and exhibits awareness of how positionality conditions both what and how communication transpires  ·       Displays a commitment to supporting first year students and a working understanding of the various challenges and opportunities that first year students at Lang can encounter ·       Possesses a broad-based investment and interest in Lang/TNS culture and community ·       Committed to (and/or open to) learning about social justice struggles and to dismantling interpersonal, institutional, and structural violence at TNS and beyond  ·       Committed to seminar learning, process-oriented pedagogy, and the relay between academic, social, and holistic wellness     Hourly Rate: $20   Work Mode: On-campus position #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: The First Year Mentor program is a leadership opportunity for Eugene Lang students to support incoming first-year students as they transition to college, fostering a community grounded in care, critical thinking, and social justice. Mentors participate in extensive training, collaborate with faculty and campus partners, develop workshop curricula, and help facilitate Orientation activities, including seminars, campus tours, and academic advising panels. Ideal candidates are strong communicators who are committed to student support, inclusive community building, social justice, and the academic mission of Lang and The New School. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Student-Ambassador-MA-Media-Studies---Student-Assistant-Specialist_JR108908": {
      "title": "Student Ambassador MA Media Studies - Student Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nSTUDENT ASSISTANT SPECIALIST - Student Ambassador The MA, Media Studies program is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented Student Assistant Specialists, student ambassador.  They serve as  the point of contact between the Program Director, Admissions staff, and prospective and admitted students.  They check a dedicated email to field questions about courses, viable lines of study and research, student life, etc.  Questions about admission policies, procedures, and requirements should be referred to the Office of Admissions. RESPONSIBILITIES The Student Assistant Specialist will: Respond to emails sent to the ambassador account for the program.  It is expected that accounts will be checked a minimum of every other day. Upon request, the ambassador will meet with prospective students, either in person by phone or virtually, at a mutually convenient time.  Responsible for arranging class visits for prospective students who are interested in them.  Attend Open House/Information Sessions, including admitted student events, to provide information from the student’s perspective to prospective students (typically once per month).  Attend monthly ambassador meetings with Admissions point of contact. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Current student in good standing at The New School. Strong organizational skills, with the ability to manage multiple tasks and meet deadlines. Effective written and verbal communication skills. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Prior experience in communications work. Prior experience in news writing and/or digital publishing. Design skills for print and digital media. ELIGIBILITY & ENROLLMENT In order to be eligible a student position in the MA, Media Studies at The New School, students must meet all the following eligibility requirements in the semester for which they would like to apply: Must be a current graduate level student. Must be registered for full-time status (9 credits/3 courses) in the semester the student would like to be considered for a position. Must be within the time limit for attaining your degree. Must be a continuing student and have achieved a minimum cumulative GPA of 3.0. Must not have more than 33% of attempted course credits as incompletes. Must not be employed at The New School as administrative staff. Must file new hire paperwork form at the University if you are a first time student employee (if selected for a position). International students must complete foreign national forms. All selected students must be authorized to work in the United States and must obtain a social security number. All students must adhere to the 20 hours per week work limit. The 20 hours includes the total amount of time for all on-campus jobs. Federal regulations limit international students to no more than 20 hours of employment per week. All students must have a social security number before obtaining employment. Hourly Rate : $20/hour. This position is 5 hours per week during the academic semester. Work Mode: Hybrid/Split – Employees hired for this position can work remotely for the majority of tasks.  Some new student events are in-person. #LI-DNI  We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS * ( if applicable) n/a   Responsibilities: Respond to emails sent to the ambassador account for the program.  It is expected that accounts will be checked a minimum of every other day. Upon request, the ambassador will meet with prospective students, either in person by phone or virtually, at a mutually convenient time. Responsible for arranging class visits for prospective students who are interested in them. Attend Open House/Information Sessions, including admitted student events, to provide information from the student’s perspective to prospective students. Attend monthly ambassador meetings with Admissions point of contact. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/JJ---39-West-13th-Street/Parsons-Fashion-Study-Collection---Student-Assistant--Specialist-_JR108897-1": {
      "title": "Parsons Fashion Study Collection - Student Assistant (Specialist)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-06-01\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nParsons’ School of Fashion (SoF) leads the industry into a future where access, equity and sustainability are the standard. We offer a Bachelor of Fine Arts degree in Fashion Design, Associate Degrees in Fashion Design as well as in Fashion Marketing and Communication, a Master of Fine Arts in Textiles, a Master of Professional Studies in Fashion Management, and a Master of Fine Arts in Fashion Design and Society. Our students, faculty, and staff are committed to supporting Indigenous resurgence; honoring the beauty of all bodies; and living in harmony with animals and the earth in ways that advance climate justice. The School of Art and Design History and Theory (ADHT) engages students at all degree levels in the analysis of art and design as essential to the formation of knowledge and culture. ADHT offers the first-year undergraduate curriculum to all Parsons students as well as a new BFA program, Design History and Practice. Graduate programs from ADHT include the MA Fashion Studies and the MA History of Design and Curatorial Studies programs. These two part-time positions and associated work is in relation to the Parsons Fashion Study Collection (PFSC). The collection of approximately 4,000 items extends from the late 19th century to the latter half of the 20th century including noted designers: Sophie Gimbel, Claire McCardell, Donald Brooks, Norman Norell, Geoffrey Beene, Giorgio di Sant'angelo and Yves Saint Laurent. The ideal candidates will demonstrate a commitment to curatorial work, handling archival fashion items, collection management and administrative tasks associated with the Parsons Fashion Study Collection (PFSC), including preparing /facilitating class visits from courses within ADHT and SoF. The candidates will report directly to the Associate Dean in the School of Fashion. RESPONSIBILITIES Primary job duties and responsibilities will include: Liaising with faculty for Parsons Fashion Study Collection (PFSC)  visits Selecting garments based on requests in preparation for class visits Facilitating class visits to the collection, schedule-permitting Returning garments to the collection at the conclusion of class visits Cataloging/Image management: Reconciling images of archived garments with the existing database Documentation of remaining images of the collection via photography  Uploading images to collection management system Past Perfect     Curating onsite exhibits in the School of Fashion Hub as needed   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Enrolled in one of the following undergraduate /graduate programs:  BFA Fashion Design, AAS Fashion Design, MA Fashion Studies, MFA Fashion Design and Society, MA History of Design and Curatorial Studies Strong verbal and written communication skills  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience working with collections and/or archives  Experience working with Past Perfect  WORK MODE On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI   Availability: Office Hours are subject to change Hourly Rate: This position is part-time and paid on an hourly basis at $20 per hour.  We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS * ( if applicable)  Resume / Cover Letter outlining expression of interest and suitability for the position Responsibilities: The primary job duties and responsibilities will include liaising with faculty for Parsons Fashion Study Collection (PFSC)  visits and cataloging/image management using Past Perfect system. It also includes curating onsite exhibitions for the School of Fashion Hub as needed. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/OCSE-Student-Assistant---Admission-Operations_JR108858": {
      "title": "OCSE Student Assistant - Admission Operations",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-12\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Admission Operations office seeks motivated students to provide general office support. Responsibilities include but are not limited to the following: Open, scan, and process incoming mail Provide administrative support to the Operations team Consolidate applicant and prospect records Perform duplicate checks for applicant records in our CRM Respond to prospective applicant inquiries via email Maintain current knowledge of admission and student services areas Assist in admission-related mailings Participate in special projects as needed Additional duties may be assigned Minimum Qualifications: Professional demeanor and ability to maintain confidentiality Excellent written and verbal communication skills Superior organizational skills Energetic, personable and team-oriented Strong work ethic; Ability to take direction and follow through on jobs until completion Experience working independently with limited hands-on supervision Ability to take the initiative and remain flexible Working knowledge of Google Suite and Microsoft Office Suite (Excel, Word). Preferred Qualifications : Preference will be given to students with Federal Work-study awards Hourly Rate : $17  Hourly Rate 10-20 hours a week   Work Mode : Hybrid/Remote  – Employees hired for this position primarily work remotely, with the occasional on-campus presence required with advanced notice. Employees in this role will also be expected to use their best judgment to be on campus when necessary in order to best fulfill the responsibilities of their job descriptions. #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce Responsibilities: The Admission Operations Student Assistant will provide administrative support to the Operations team. They will be expected to perform duplicate checks for applicant records in our CRM, answer student emails in a professional manor and other duties as assigned. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/OCSE-Student-Assistant---Welcome-Center_JR108841": {
      "title": "OCSE Student Assistant - Welcome Center",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-05-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School is looking for enthusiastic, outgoing students to join our team as Student Assistants within the University Welcome Center. Our Student Assistants facilitate in-person campus tours and participate in virtual programs and events designed to help prospective students and their families learn more about The New School’s academic programs, social life, and application requirements. They also serve as a first point of contact for visitors to campus as receptionists staffing the Welcome Center front desk and contribute content to the Welcome Center Instagram account, online admitted student communities, and New School Parent and Family Hub. Responsibilities: Acting as representatives of the university, warmly welcoming all campus visitors and establishing a quality first impression.  Displaying pride and passion for The New School Maintaining up-to-date information about our academic programs, student services, and admission requirements Consistently representing themselves and the university in a genuine, professional, and inclusive manner. Hourly Rate : The rate for this position is $19/hr. Work Mode :  Hybrid/Split - Employees hired for this position have regularly scheduled, consistent percentage of time on campus (ex 1-4x/week) and also work some of the time remotely. #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.​ Responsibilities: Our Student Assistants facilitate in-person campus tours and participate in virtual programs and events designed to help prospective students and their families learn more about The New School’s academic programs, social life, and application requirements. They also serve as a first point of contact for visitors to campus as receptionists staffing the Welcome Center front desk and contribute content to the Welcome Center Instagram account, online admitted student communities, and New School Parent and Family Hub. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/U---63-Fifth-Avenue/FWS-Archives-Page--Student-Assistant-_JR108808": {
      "title": "FWS Archives Page (Student Assistant)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-21\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School Archives and Special Collections–a unit of the New School Libraries, Collections and Academic Services (LCAS)–seeks 7-12 students with Federal Work Study awards to serve as Archives Pages. The Archives Page will work under the supervision of the archivists to retrieve boxes from on-site storage, prepare for research appointments and class visits, transfer Special Collections books to other library spaces, and be a welcoming first point of contact for visitors conducting research in the Archives. Open to students with Federal Work Study awards only , this is an on-campus position starting in September 2026. Students, with the approval of the supervisor, will establish a regular schedule of 4-8 hours a week, between Monday and Friday, 9 am to 5:30 pm. Once established, the student must maintain a consistent schedule and commit to the position for the entire semester, preferably with the intention of remaining in the position throughout the academic year. Preference will be given to students in the early stages of their academic program.  RESPONSIBILITIES Locating, retrieving, and preparing archival materials requested by patrons Shelving materials after staff use, research appointments, and class visits  Open or close the Research Room on weekdays, in addition to proctoring research appointments Communicating and enforcing Research Room policies and procedures to users in a courteous manner Engaging directly with archives visitors by answering in-person inquiries and referring visitors to appropriate place or person for assistance Assisting researchers with basic computer, internet and audio/visual equipment usage during appointments when necessary MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Matriculated students with Federal Work Study awards, who can maintain a consistent schedule for the entire semester. Strong communication skills and ability to follow oral and written instructions in fast-paced environment. Demonstrated reliability, professionalism, and punctuality. Superior English written and oral communication skills. Ability to accurately follow precise written and oral instructions. Facility to work independently, with minimal supervision. Physical ability and willingness to lift boxes up to 50 lbs, push loaded book carts, and sit at a desk for extended periods.   PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Excellent customer service skills and the ability to interact with visitors internal and external to the university. Basic computer and basic technology skills such as Microsoft Office and Google Suite applications. Familiarity with Google Suite (Calendar, Gmail, Docs, Sheets, etc.) and Microsoft Office. HOURLY RATE: $17/hour WORK MODE On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Special instructions: Applicants must submit a resume and letter of interest. The letter of interest should demonstrate the ability to write professionally and concisely. Responsibilities: The Student Archives Page will assist with public-facing services, under the supervision of the New School Archives and Special Collections staff. Student is expected to set up for research appointments, serve as a clerk during research visits to archives, retrieve collections, and prepare materials for transfer to other offices. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Gig-Performer--Senior-Student-Assistant-Specialist_JR108561": {
      "title": "Gig Performer, Senior Student Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-15\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Gig Performer, Senior Student Assistant Specialist College of Performing Arts Position Availability: This position is available starting immediately and will accept applications on a rolling basis. Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries, offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts. Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The College of Performing Arts at The New School seeks highly motivated student musicians to serve as Gig Performer, Senior Student Assistant Specialists. We’re looking for energetic, creative, and responsible individuals to support live performance initiatives across all divisions at the College of Performing Arts. This is an ideal position for students at the College of Performing Arts who are interested in a career as a working musician. Performance opportunities through the School of Jazz & Contemporary Music and The College of Performing Gig Office will be scheduled through the Program & Administration Manager, School of Jazz & Contemporary Music and the Part-Time Operations Manager, School of Jazz & Contemporary Music. Performance opportunities through the Mannes School of Music will be scheduled through the Dean, Mannes School of Music; Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, Mannes School of Music; Program and Administration Manager, Mannes School of Music; and/or the Performance and Ensemble Manager. Performance opportunities through Mannes Prep will be scheduled through the Director, Mannes Prep; and the Assistant Director, Mannes Prep. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES School of Jazz & Contemporary Music and The College of Performing Gig Office: Provide instrumental and/or vocal performance services for public or private events. Analyze assigned music prior to rehearsal and performances (e.g., correct tempos, challenging transitions, dynamics) to ensure efficient use of rehearsal time. Exhibit professionalism in all interactions with internal and external parties. Respond to inquiries from students or staff in a timely manner regarding performance opportunities. Adhere to departmental guidelines regarding reporting hours, payroll deadlines, and other items. Mannes School of Music: Perform for curricular and extracurricular performance opportunities as assigned, including but not limited to: Collaborative Skills courses, Techniques of Conducting courses, Mannes Outreach Events, Admitted Students Events, Staff Piano Auditions, Commencement Activities, and more. Exhibit professionalism in all interactions with internal and external parties. Prepare music as assigned by Mannes School of Music faculty, staff, and leadership, ensuring efficient use of class/rehearsal time, and success of performances. Adhere to departmental guidelines regarding reporting hours, payroll deadlines, and other items. Mannes Prep: Attend Mannes Prep rehearsals and performances as directed. Learn assigned music prior to all services with Mannes Prep ensembles. Exhibit professionalism in all interactions with students, faculty, staff, and audience members. Respond to inquiries from the Mannes Prep office in a timely manner regarding rehearsal and performance schedules.  Adhere to departmental guidelines regarding reporting hours, payroll deadlines, and other items. QUALIFICATIONS Enrolled in a degree program at the College of Performing Arts. Ability to provide evidence of advanced musicianship. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Performances may occur in offsite venues. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $20.00 - $100.00, variable depending on the gig. Hours per Week: Scheduled on an as-needed basis, variable commitment with no guaranteed hours. Not to exceed 20 hours in a single workweek. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their interest, skills, and experience pertaining to this position. Applicants will be contacted if the need for their services arises. Responsibilities: Provide instrumental and/or vocal performance services for events, preparing assigned music in advance to ensure productive rehearsals and high-quality performances. Maintain professionalism in all interactions, respond promptly to inquiries, and comply with departmental policies and administrative requirements. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Student-Assistant-Specialist--BFA-Photo-Events-End-of-Year-_JR108796": {
      "title": "Student Assistant Specialist (BFA Photo Events/End of Year)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-13\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe BFA Photography program is seeking a knowledgeable, dedicated, and enthusiastic student to join our team supporting programmatic events and End of Year festivities. This person will be working closely with program leadership and the program administrator, supporting the program on internal curricular events, including year-based Critique Days and the end-of-year Thesis Exhibition. RESPONSIBILITIES Primary duties for this position include: Support the BFA Photography Program in all public events, including the Visiting Artist lecture series and End of Year festivities. Help with setup and breakdown of events. Create visual marketing materials (posters) for public and curricular events. Design and print wall labels for BFA Photography Thesis Exhibition. Update the BFA Photography Thesis website with student works. Support BFA Photography Thesis Exhibition installation and de-installation. Help to direct students in the gallery space during drop-off and pick-up. Attend, when possible, programmatic events. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Fluency in the Adobe Creative Suite (particularly InDesign). Design skills to create posters / flyers for public and program events. Strong communication skills and responsiveness to emails. Timely submission of work. Strong work ethic.    WORK MODE ●  Hybrid - Employees hired for this position primarily work remotely with the occasional on-campus presence required with advanced notice. Employees in this role will also be expected to use their best judgment to be on campus when necessary in order to best fulfill the responsibilities of their job descriptions. #LI-DNI   HOURLY RATE $21 per hour 5-10 hours a week for 5 weeks   We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: In this position the responsibilities include building out the BFA Photo Thesis website pages for each graduating student and uploading the images and text. As well as utilizing InDesign to support the production of materials for the BFA Photography Thesis exhibition.  We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/B---65-West-11th-Street/Student-Assistant-Specialist_JR108778": {
      "title": "Student Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-10\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Student Assistant Specialist will help troubleshoot technical issues that arise and support the professor in demonstrating equipment usage. RESPONSIBILITIES Check out equipment at the beginning of class Charge batteries at the beginning of class Test batteries at the beginning of class Test cameras at the beginning of class Test sound equipment at the beginning of class Clean lenses throughout class Demonstrate use of equipment throughout class Return equipment at the end of class MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with camera equipment Familiarity with sound equipment Familiarity with lighting equipment Familiarity with editing software WORK MODE On-Campus Position #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $17 per hour We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Assisting the professor in demonstrating how to use the equipment, maintaining the equipment, and helping the students with editing questions.   We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Creative--Artistic--and-Production-Staff_JR108557": {
      "title": "Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-04-02\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The College of Performing Arts at The New School is seeking highly qualified Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff to join its Production team. Reporting to the Vice Dean of Performing Arts and leadership of the Production & Performance Operations team, the College of Performing Arts’ Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff are directly responsible for providing high-quality, professional theatrical services that guarantee the success of the College’s curricular productions. Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff shape and execute the artistic vision of their assigned productions. They coordinate design, staging, and technical elements to ensure rehearsals and performances run smoothly. Through close collaboration with our students, staff, and faculty, Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff maintain consistency in artistic quality throughout all stages of the production process. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This position does not have regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Production department. Temporary Creative, Artistic, and Production Staff will receive a Memorandum of Understanding, outlining the terms and conditions for all services they are scheduled for. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide creative and/or logistical support to curricular theatrical productions as assigned. Ensure any relevant deliverables are generated meeting the Production’s deadlines Coordinate with department heads and leadership as necessary. Communicate and collaborate with all stakeholders, attending all required meetings. Additional responsibilities, expectations, and deadlines tailored to each individual engagement will be outlined in a Memorandum of Understanding. QUALIFICATIONS Demonstrated experience in theatrical production, stage management, design, direction, or related support roles. Strong organizational, communication, and collaboration skills. Ability to manage multiple priorities in fast-paced, deadline-driven environments. Knowledge of standard theatrical practices, safety protocols, and production workflows. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Prior experience working in academic or higher education environments WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Hybrid work arrangements may be considered on a case-by-case basis, depending on the nature of the role and operational needs. Any such arrangement must be discussed and approved in advance by the appropriate division lead or their designee. SALARY RANGE $25.00-$50.00/hour, dependent upon the nature of the engagement WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Large-Ensemble-Ringer_JR108768": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Large Ensemble Ringer",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Performance Operations area at The New School’s College of Performing Arts is seeking highly qualified Overhire Large Ensemble Ringers to join its team. Reporting to the Large Ensemble Manager, the Overhire Large Ensemble Ringer supports initiatives within the Performance Operations - Large Ensembles area on an as-needed basis. This includes Mannes Orchestra, Mannes American Composers Ensemble, Mannes Opera Orchestra, and other ensembles. This position reports to the Manager of Large Ensembles.  Alumni of the College of Performing Arts are strongly encouraged to apply. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Large Ensemble department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Attend all the rehearsals and performances as scheduled with the assigned ensemble Bring one’s own instrument(s) and gear as needed Analyze assigned music prior to rehearsal and performances (e.g., correct tempos, challenging transitions, dynamics) to ensure efficient use of rehearsal time Exhibit professionalism in all interactions with students, faculty, staff, and audience members Be prepared to play professionally with one’s assigned part Adhere to departmental guidelines regarding reporting hours, payroll deadlines, and other items including attire.  QUALIFICATIONS Classically trained musician Ability to play all assigned instruments, including auxiliaries Prior orchestral/large ensemble experience.  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with contemporary and non-traditional scores, including opera. Alumni of the College of Performing Arts WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-Onsite Hours per Week: Up to 15 hours per week, per cycle, variable commitment with no guaranteed hours. Rehearsals are typically on weekdays 1 pm to 3:50 pm, with some nights and/ or weekends as needed. SALARY RANGE Hourly Rate: $55.00/hour Rehearsals (Up to 3 hours): $165.00 per service  Dress Rehearsals (Up to 4 hours): $220.00 per service Concerts (Up to 4 hours): $220.00 per service Any work above minimum call is paid at $55.00/hour WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Z---151-Bank-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Scenic-Artist_JR108766": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Scenic Artist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-30\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The College of Performing Arts at The New School is seeking a highly qualified Overhire Scenic Artist to join its Performance Operations – Scenic Department Staff. The Scenic Department is responsible for the creation, alteration, and sourcing of all scenery for productions in the Mannes School of Music, School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and School of Drama. The Overhire Scenic Artist is delegated as needed to work on completion and finishing of scenic builds. The Overhire Scenic Artist is a qualified and organized collaborator who can follow instructions, work independently, and thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, and highly team-oriented environment. The Overhire Scenic Artist reports to the Production Shops Manager.   This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Scenic department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as a painter to assist the Scenic Charge Artist complete tasks as needed.  Carry out duties assigned by Scenic Charge or Production Shops Manager. Maintain a clean paint area in the prop shop and clean up at end of day Work alongside carpenters for space management and build completion Apply painting techniques to scenery  Ensure proper fire retardancy is being added to paint and scenery as needed/described by the Production shops manager  Additional duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with theatrical painting techniques Comfortability working alone and asking questions for clarification Ability to read a scale rule Experience working as a theatrical scenic painter WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Some weekends and weeknights may be scheduled as needed and defined by the production tech schedules. #LI-Onsite Hourly Rate: $30.00/hour WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position, and an artistic portfolio or website of samples. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Z---151-Bank-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Driver---Trucking-Hand_JR108764": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Driver & Trucking Hand",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-27\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nAt The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. The College of Performing Arts at The New School is seeking a highly qualified Overhire Driver & Trucking Hand to join its Performance Operations – Scenic Department Staff. The Scenic Department is responsible for the creation, alteration, and sourcing of all scenery for productions in the Mannes School of Music, School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and School of Drama. The Overhire Driver & Trucking Hand is delegated as needed to work on storage pulls, and/ or shopping runs. The Overhire Driver & Trucking Hand is a qualified and organized collaborator who can follow instructions, work independently, and thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, and highly team-oriented environment. The Overhire Lead Driver reports to the Production Shops Manager.  This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Scenic department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Operate truck for storage pulls and/or shopping runs or serve as a passenger in the truck to assist with loading and unloading Maintain clean usable area at storage unit  Ensure buildings and rental equipment are well maintained during shifts Use safe moving practices to ensure no one is putting themselves at risk of injury in lifting and moving things Additional duties as assigned Track receipts as necessary QUALIFICATIONS Comfort driving a box truck in Manhattan Ability to lift 50lbs comfortably State issued Driver's License, if driving  Knowledge of NYC driving regulations regarding commercial vehicles and parking  PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Strong communication skills and ability to work with other crew members collaboratively WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-Onsite Work calls may include shifts scheduled for early in the morning and on weekends as needed, and may require flexibility to coordinate short term calls SALARY RANGE $27.00/hour  WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position, and a copy of a Driver License for administration to have on file.  We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Jazz-Video---Lights--Student-Assistant-Specialist_JR108664": {
      "title": "Jazz Video & Lights, Student Assistant Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Jazz Video & Lights, Student Assistant Specialist School of Jazz and Contemporary Music College of Performing Arts Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The School of Jazz and Contemporary Music at the College of Performing Arts seeks highly motivated students to serve as Jazz Video & Lights, Student Assistant Specialist . We’re looking for an enthusiastic and reliable individual(s) to support initiatives within The School of Jazz and Contemporary Music . This position reports to the Part Time Operations Manager and is an ideal position for students who are interested in a career in lighting design, video production, or live event production. This position is open to student applicants with Federal Work Study awards, as well as student applicants without a Federal Work Study award. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Manage lighting setup and operation for live events and performances. Operate and manage live streaming for events hosted on the College of Performing Arts YouTube channel. Set up and break down audio and video equipment before and after performances. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to ensure the successful execution of performances and events. Maintain a professional and supportive presence during rehearsals and live shows. QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with video live streaming tools and techniques. Basic understanding of lighting setup and management. Strong organizational and file management skills. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and weekends as needed. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS   Recipient of Federal Work Study award. Previous experience in live sound, lighting, or video production. Knowledge of advanced lighting techniques and video production equipment. WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $18.00 Hours per Week : 3-20, or as needed. Not to exceed 20 hours in a single workweek. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit both a resume and cover letter outlining their interest, skills, and experience pertaining to this position; and a Federal Work Study award letter if applicable. Position Availability: This position is available starting 3/5/2026 and will be open until filled. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Manage lighting, audio-visual setup, and live streaming for College of Performing Arts events and performances, including equipment setup and breakdown. Collaborate with faculty, staff, and students to ensure the smooth and professional execution of rehearsals, live shows, and streamed events. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/COPA-Auditions-Student-Assistant--2nd-Wave-_JR108591": {
      "title": "COPA Auditions Student Assistant (2nd Wave)",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-24\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe Student Assistant plays a key role in supporting the audition process for applicants to The College of Performing Arts that starts on February 27th and runs until March 8th. As an integral part of the admission team, you will serve as a friendly, welcoming presence for auditionees, offering both logistical support and positive encouragement throughout the audition day. You will help ensure that auditions run smoothly and efficiently, while providing applicants with a high-quality experience at The New School. This position ends on March 8th. Applicants must be currently enrolled in a degree program at The New School for Spring 2025 and preference will be given to students enrolled in The College of Performing Arts.  KEY RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with Schedule Management: Help maintain and update a shared audition schedule to ensure smooth communication and coordination among the admission team and fellow student assistants. Assist with Check-In: Help with check-in procedures at the beginning of the audition day, ensuring that all applicants are registered, informed, and prepared. Provide General Information: Greet applicants warmly and assist with answering general questions about the university, academic programs, student services, and campus life. Escort Applicants: Accompany auditioning students to their warm-up rooms and auditions, providing them with a clear and calm experience as they prepare for their audition. Support the Admissions Team: Work closely with the performing arts admissions staff, providing assistance wherever needed, including logistical tasks, troubleshooting, or filling in to support the team. Represent The New School: Act as a representative of the university, maintaining a professional, approachable demeanor at all times. Help create a positive first impression for all visitors and applicants, both online and in-person. Promote Inclusivity and Respect: Demonstrate respect, empathy, and professionalism while working with a diverse group of applicants, faculty, staff, and visitors. Ensure that all individuals feel valued and welcomed. QUALIFICATIONS Strong Interpersonal Skills: Ability to engage with a diverse range of applicants and visitors in a friendly and welcoming manner. Organizational Skills: Ability to maintain a shared schedule and handle multiple tasks in a fast-paced environment. Professionalism: Strong communication skills and the ability to represent The New School with pride, both in-person and online. Team Player: Comfortable working collaboratively with other Student Audition Assistants and the admissions team to ensure smooth operations. Passion for The New School: A genuine enthusiasm for The College of Performing Arts and its academic and extracurricular offerings. WORK MODE This position requires in-person attendance during audition days, starting on February 27th and running until March 8th - includes weekends. Flexibility and a proactive attitude are key to providing applicants with a seamless experience.  #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $17 per hour We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. Responsibilities: Student Assistants will assist with scheduling, check-In, and provide general information to applicants during COPA auditions week. Students will work closely with the performing arts admission staff, providing assistance wherever needed, including logistical tasks, troubleshooting, or filling in to support the team.  Students will be expected to represent The New School and ensure that all visitors feel welcomed. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/H---72-Fifth-Avenue/COPA-Auditions-Student-Assistant_JR108542": {
