    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-House-Manager_JR108586-1": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire House Manager",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Overhire House Manager Performance Operations - Front of House College of Performing Arts INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The Front of House area at The New School’s College of Performing Arts is seeking  highly qualified Overhire House Managers to join its team. Reporting to the Manager of Event Operations, the Overhire House Manager is directly responsible for the patron experience at on-site events. This role oversees ushers on-site, liaises with production staff, fields patron and performance-related issues that arise, and ensures that venues are safe and clean. The House Manager is responsible for creating an excellent experience for patrons, serving as the point person for ushers and performers, and overseeing fire code compliance in performance spaces. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Front of House department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Provide excellent customer service to patrons Maintain safe and clean public spaces, communicate with facilities and campus safety as necessary Ensure fire code compliance in performance spaces and provide leadership in emergency situations Serve as the point person for ushers’ scheduling and event-specific duties Coordinate performance timelines with relevant parties (stage management, performers, faculty, audio/video staff, etc) Oversee audience check in, distribution of programs, and audience seating Work with production staff to meet event-specific needs Resolve on-site issues and conflicts, documenting incidents as needed Complete a house report for each event worked Additional responsibilities as assigned QUALIFICATIONS 2 years of experience in live performance events Previous experience in customer service roles A background in the performing arts, especially music and/or theater Demonstrated commitment to Equity, Inclusion, Social Justice, and the transformative power of the arts and education PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS   Bachelor’s Degree or equivalent professional experience. Previous House Management experience Active F-03 Fireguard Certification WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Nights and weekends are required. SALARY RANGE $22.00/hour  WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume and a cover letter outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/B---65-West-11th-Street/New-School-New-Books-Presenter_JR108748": {
      "title": "New School New Books Presenter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nBased on contributions to a New School publication, participation in this year's iteration of New School New Books , the annual reading series fourth edition on Friday, February 20, 2026, in Wollman Hall.  New School New Books was introduced by the VLC in 2023 and most recently convened this past March, to celebrate recent publications by university centers, faculty, and students. The 2026 edition comes together with a slightly different focus—highlighting various publishing platforms and periodicals directed by TNS faculty, students, and staff. We are choosing \"periodicals\" as a curatorial frame to respond to the setting: Wollman Hall will feature a new installation of 16 prints by legendary artist Robert Rauschenberg (1925–2008) that focus on and incorporate references to \"the news.\" Offering an apt prompt for the current moment, these prints are part of The New School Art Collection. The gathering will showcase the rich body of print and digital newspapers, journals, magazines, and other periodicals published by members of the university community. We invite representatives from these publications to join us for a series of informal, conversational panels throughout the day on the urgent need for journalism and how on-campus publishing platforms can offer timely, in-depth responses to some of the most socially, institutionally and politically pressing issues we face today. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.   Key Responsibilities: Present a clear and engaging 5–8 minute overview of your publication, including its mission, editorial focus, and recent work. Represent your journal as a knowledgeable contributor, offering insight into its role within campus publishing and broader public discourse. Participate actively in panel discussions, contributing thoughtful perspectives on journalism and responding to audience or moderator questions. Collaborate with event organizers and fellow presenters to ensure smooth timing, coordination, and flow of the program. Engage professionally with attendees and remain present throughout the event to support its collaborative and conversational format. Qualifications : - Currently enrolled at TNS and on staff/contributor/editor at one of the journals  or publications that were solicited for participation. Hourly Rate : $20/hr Work mode : Hybrid #LI-DNI Responsibilities: Present a clear and engaging 5–8 minute overview of your publication, including its mission, editorial focus, and recent work. Represent your journal as a knowledgeable contributor, offering insight into its role within campus publishing and broader public discourse. Participate actively in panel discussions, contributing thoughtful perspectives on journalism and responding to audience or moderator questions. Collaborate with event organizers and fellow presenters to ensure smooth timing, coordination, and flow of the program. Engage professionally with attendees and remain present throughout the event to support its collaborative and conversational format. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Illustration-Senior-Show-Student-Workers_JR108683": {
      "title": "Illustration Senior Show Student Workers",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-19\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nThe New School was founded by forward-thinking educators in 1919 to defy the intellectual constraints of a traditional college education. BFA Illustration is seeking a student employee to support the BFA Illustration Senior Show. Applicants must be seniors in the Illustration program. In addition, students must have strong organizational skills and attention to detail; be able to carefully transport and handle artwork and materials; print posters; be familiar with Google Spreadsheets; and communicate responsibly with Professors Jordin Isip and Rodger Stevens, the Senior Show Coordinators. Support the Senior Show Coordinating Faculty Jordin Isip and Rodger Stevens. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with the intake of Seniors’ artwork and promotional materials on Fri, March 6 Catalog the received student exhibition materials on Google Spreadsheets Transfer artwork and exhibition materials from the Illustration Office to Kellen Gallery Prepare artwork and materials for installation Assist with the installation of artwork, exhibition materials, promotional cards, labels, statements, and exhibition signage to the walls Create and print promotions, posters and flyers for the exhibition Set up the catering for the  Tue, March 17th opening reception Assist with the de-installation of artwork and other exhibition materials MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Provide a bulleted list of the minimum qualifications that are necessary for someone to be considered for the position. All qualifications must comply with applicable state and Federal legislation. Acceptable qualifications include: Education, specialized knowledge Skills, Abilities, and other professional attributes that are relevant to the work Professional Certification Experience Schedule requirements outside of regular business hours PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS You may also wish to indicate additional qualifications beyond those above that are not absolutely required but that will help candidates distinguish themselves – specific skills, advanced degrees, etc. WORK MODE On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI Hourly Rate:  21.00/hr Responsibilities: The students will assist with the intake of Seniors’ artwork and promotional materials for Senior Show, catalog the received student exhibition materials on Google Spreadsheets, transfer artwork and exhibition materials from the Illustration Office to Kellen Gallery, prepare artwork and materials for installation, assist with the installation of artwork, exhibition materials, promotional cards, labels, statements, and exhibition signage to the walls, create and print promotions, posters and flyers for the exhibition, set up the catering for the opening reception and assist with the de-installation of artwork and other exhibition materials We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/L---2-West-13th-Street/Senior-Student-Assistant-Specialist-SJDC-Galleries_JR108549": {
      "title": "Senior Student Assistant Specialist SJDC Galleries",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-18\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE: Senior Student Assistant Specialist SJDC Galleries The Sheila C. Johnson Design Center (SJDC) galleries at Parsons/The New School are looking for a Senior Student Assistant Specialist to help with exhibition planning and installation across our two campus galleries. Reporting to the Assistant Director, this role includes hands-on support with layout, installation, and preparing all gallery text and print materials. The work involves using special printers and professional grade paper, and may include decisions about how the gallery space is used for artwork. We’re looking for someone who has experience or coursework in art installation, curating, or gallery work and who can work independently in a fast-paced, collaborative environment. RESPONSIBILITIES Help plan exhibition layouts alongside the Assistant Director. Support decisions about artwork placement and how the space flows. Install artworks using safe and proper handling methods. Use specialized printers and paper to prepare wall labels, text, and printed materials. Assist with mounting and installing all printed items in the gallery. Help with production, fabrication, and overall install process. Provide support with schedules, logistics, and general gallery needs during install. Take on other duties related to exhibitions as needed. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Experience working in galleries or with exhibition installation. Able to use hand tools (like drills, levels, saws, etc.) safely. Comfortable making layout and setup decisions independently. Knows how to format and print professional materials for gallery use. Able to work flexible hours, including evenings or weekends during installs. Works well both alone and with a team. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience or coursework in art installation, curating, or gallery operations. Confidence using tools, ladders, and handling delicate artworks. Ability to work both independently and as part of a team. Interest in exhibitions, design, and how shows come together. WORK MODE On-Campus Position - Employees in this position are expected to work on-campus during regularly scheduled work hours due to the nature of the work being that which is not feasible, or not in the best interest of the organization, to be performed remotely. #LI-DNI HOURLY RATE $24.13 per hour SPECIAL INSTRUCTION TO APPLICANTS If you require additional documents outside of a Resume or Cover Letter (i.e. a writing sample), please include details specifying what those documents are. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce.   Responsibilities: This student role supports exhibition planning and installation by assisting with layout decisions, artwork placement, and ensuring safe handling of works. The position also involves preparing and installing printed materials, supporting production and logistics during install, and helping with overall gallery operations as needed. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Carpenter_JR108733": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Carpenter",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-17\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Overhire Carpenter Performance Operations - Theater & Opera College of Performing Arts INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The College of Performing Arts at The New School is seeking a highly qualified Overhire Carpenter to join its Performance Operations – Scenic Department Staff. The Scenic Department is responsible for the creation, alteration, and sourcing of all scenery for productions in the Mannes School of Music, School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and School of Drama. The Overhire Carpenter is delegated as needed to work on builds, load ins and strikes.  The Overhire Carpenter is a qualified and organized collaborator who can follow instructions, work independently, and thrive in a dynamic, fast-paced, and highly team-oriented environment. The Overhire Carpenter reports to the Production Shops Manager.  This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the Scenic department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Serve as a general hand called in to work with the Scenic Department and carry out tasks as assigned including cross-department work as assigned by the Production Shops Manager or Temporary Lead Carpenter Assist loading and unloading scenery into and out of performance venues Work in production shops to construct scenery Use ladders and genies in performance spaces to hang soft goods Occasionally use sewing machines as needed for scenic soft good repairs and builds Maintain a safe and clean work environment during build and load in processes  Additional duties as assigned QUALIFICATIONS Familiarity with some or many tools in a wood working setting Ability to lift 50lbs comfortably  Experience as a stagehand or carpenter in other institutions WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. Some weekends and weeknights may be scheduled as needed and defined by the ongoing production tech schedules SALARY RANGE $27.00/hour WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Jazz-A2_JR108656": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Jazz A2",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Overhire Jazz A2 School of Jazz and Contemporary Music College of Performing Arts INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The School of Jazz and Contemporary Music at The New School’s College of Performing Arts is seeking highly qualified Overhire Jazz A2 to join its team. Reporting to the Part Time Operations Manager, the Overhire Jazz A2 is responsible for supporting the Audio and Video needs of academic performances and partnership events within the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music.  The Overhire Jazz A2 provides crucial support in the successful execution of concerts, panel discussions, and festivals at the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music. This position is responsible for assisting with setup, operation, and breakdown of audio systems, as well as serving as a key crew member during events. The Overhire Jazz A2 works under the direction of the Overhire Jazz A1 and reports to the Part-Time Operations Manager, School of Jazz and Contemporary Music. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Assist with the setup, operation, and strike of all audio equipment for performances and events Support the Overhire Jazz A1 during soundchecks and live events, including managing microphones, monitors, playback, and communication systems Maintain and troubleshoot wired and wireless microphones, IEM systems, and backline as needed Follow and execute technical documentation including input lists, stage plots, signal flow diagrams, and run-of-show documents Provide professional and courteous support to performers, faculty, and production staff Maintain organization and cleanliness of audio equipment and performance spaces Mix smaller events independently, including recording sessions, and rehearsals as scheduled  Additional responsibilities as assigned by the Overhire Jazz A1, or the Part-Time Operations Manager QUALIFICATIONS At least 1 year of experience working on live events in a support role (A2, Audio Technician, etc.) Familiarity with live sound systems, microphones, cabling, and digital consoles (Yamaha, Allen & Heath, Midas, Behringer) Working knowledge of basic audio signal flow and gain structure Some experience with audio-related software (QLab, Wireless Workbench, Dante Controller, Dante Virtual Soundcard) Ability to read and follow event documentation including input lists and stage plots Strong communication, reliability, and collaborative skills Ability to work calmly and efficiently under pressure during live events Comfortable working with students, faculty, and a diverse production team Ability to adhere to university COVID-19 policy and requirements Commitment to Equity, Inclusion, Social Justice, and the transformative power of the arts and education PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS   Experience working in music, theater, or academic environments Familiarity with Dante networks Comfortable working at heights and using ladders or lifts FO3 Fireguard Certification Ability to lift up to 50 lbs Self-motivated and detail-oriented WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. SALARY RANGE $28.00/hour  WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    },
    "https://newschool.wd1.myworkdayjobs.com/job/I---55-West-13th-Street/Temporary-Overhire-Jazz-A1_JR108655": {
      "title": "Temporary Overhire Jazz A1",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-03-05\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nPart time\n\nPOSITION TITLE Overhire Jazz A1 School of Jazz and Contemporary Music College of Performing Arts INTRODUCTORY PARAGRAPH Join The New School  At The New School, we redefine the boundaries of education, creativity, and innovation. Founded in 1919 and located in the heart of New York City, we are home to over 9,000 students from over 100 countries , offering more than 135 degree and diploma programs across our renowned colleges, including Parsons School of Design, The New School for Social Research, Eugene Lang college of Liberal Arts, Parsons Paris, and the College of Performing Arts . Our progressive, interdisciplinary approach has earned us recognition as one of the most forward-thinking institutions in the world. POSITION/ROLE OVERVIEW The School of Jazz and Contemporary Music at The New School’s College of Performing Arts is seeking highly qualified Overhire Jazz A1 to join its team. Reporting to the Part Time Operations Manager, the Overhire Jazz A1is responsible for supporting the Audio and Video needs of academic performances and partnership events within the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music.  The A1 is responsible for the overall sound quality of live events and live streams, including concerts, panel discussions, and festivals across all schools within the College of Performing Arts. The A1 also leads and directs the audio crew during crew calls as needed. This position reports to the Part-Time Operations Manager, School of Jazz and Contemporary Music. Formed in 2015, the College of Performing Arts draws together the Mannes School of Music, the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music, and the School of Drama. College of Performing Arts students are actors, musicians, performers, writers, improvisers, creative technologists, entrepreneurs, composers, arts managers, and multidisciplinary artists. Our community collaborates with colleagues across The New School in a wide array of disciplines, from the visual arts and fashion design, to the social sciences, public policy, advocacy, and more. This is an overhire position without regular or guaranteed weekly hours. Opportunities for work will be scheduled on an as-needed basis by the School of Jazz and Contemporary Music department. This position may be renewed pending institutional need and availability of funding. CORE CAPABILITIES, PRIMARY DUTIES, AND RESPONSIBILITIES Understand and execute the technical aspects of each design, including interpreting audio needs, signal flow plans, I/O lists, and stage plots. Mix Front of House (FOH), monitors, and streaming audio feeds, occasionally simultaneously on the same console. Provide professional and courteous service to all parties. Fulfill the role of System Technician, Console Operator, or both, depending on the size and scope of the event. Manage setup, operation, and strike of equipment before, during, and after events. This includes operating audio consoles, playback systems, and all related audio gear. Supervise and direct Audio Technicians to ensure completion of required tasks and delivery of the CoPA standard. Provide guidance and leadership as needed. Perform additional responsibilities as assigned. QUALIFICATIONS At least 1 year of experience as a live sound engineer for concerts, corporate events  or theater Live-mixing skills and working knowledge of digital consoles, specifically, Yamaha, Allen & Heath, Midas, and Behringer Excellent knowledge of proper gain structure and signal flow Working knowledge of audio related software, such as Qlab 4&5, Wireless Workbench 6, Pro Tools, Logic. Dante Virtual Soundcard, Dante Controller, etc. Ability to interpret event technical documents including technical riders, signal flow diagrams, input lists, stage plots, run-of-show, and cue lists. Strong verbal and written communication, organization, and time-management skills Ability to communicate with other departments and event coordinator to ensure a smooth show. Punctuality, professionalism, and a positive collaborative attitude when working with Students, Faculty, Staff, and Team Members.  Experienced or able to learn and develop fluency in The New School’s suite of applications including Google Suite, Microsoft Office, and WorkDay. Ability to adhere to university COVID-19 policy and requirements Demonstrated commitment to Equity, Inclusion, Social Justice, and the transformative power of the arts and education PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Corporate, Special Events, Festival Sound, Line by Line Musical Mixing, and Broadcast experience are all plusses  Self-motivated with ability to work with minimal supervision Ability to safely climb ladders and scaffolding, operate Genies, and comfortable working at heights Able to lift up to 50lbs WORK MODE This position is primarily in-person and is based on campus to support effective in-person collaboration and engagement. SALARY RANGE $35.00/hour  WHY JOIN US? This is an extraordinary opportunity to work closely with a visionary leader and contribute meaningfully to a forward-thinking institution that’s reshaping the future of higher education. You’ll be at the nexus of strategy, operations, and innovation in a role that grows with your impact. We are an equal opportunity employer and do not discriminate in hiring or employment on the basis of race, color, creed, religion or belief, national or ethnic origin, citizenship status, marital or domestic partnership status, sexual orientation, sex, gender identity or expression, age, disability, military or veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local law. The New School recognizes and values the benefits of a diverse workforce. SPECIAL INSTRUCTIONS TO APPLICANTS Applicants should submit a resume outlining their skills and experience concerning this position. We look forward to receiving your application!"
    }
